  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788514",
      "title": "Property Binding & Outputting Computed Values",
      "lectureOrder": 23,
      "videoOrder": 20,
      "sourceHash": "682fa8b012bbee512028d8358e70617d7999a3bf1f0ffa9484d5a4e955a18785",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 2.67,
          "en": "Now string interpolation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.67,
          "end": 4.44,
          "en": "with the double curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.44,
          "end": 8.85,
          "en": "is one of the key features offered by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.85,
          "end": 12.42,
          "en": "when it comes to outputting content in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.42,
          "end": 17.42,
          "en": "Another crucial syntax or feature offered by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.97,
          "end": 21.54,
          "en": "is the so-called property binding syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.54,
          "end": 23.85,
          "en": "Because we of course also wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.85,
          "end": 27.15,
          "en": "that we show an image of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.15,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "and for that, we need to set the src attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 31.863,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.03,
          "end": 35.04,
          "en": "Now, you could indeed do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.04,
          "end": 38.13,
          "en": "by also using the double curly braces syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.13,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "between those quotes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 43.2,
          "en": "because you can use it anywhere in your template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.2,
          "end": 46.74,
          "en": "not just between tags as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.74,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "So you could then access selectedUser.avatar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "And if you would do that and save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "you should see some output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 58.86,
          "en": "Actually not the image yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 61.98,
          "en": "because the path is not entirely correct yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.98,
          "end": 64.263,
          "en": "but you see that something changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.52,
          "end": 69.42,
          "en": "However, you would typically not use string interpolation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.42,
          "end": 72.09,
          "en": "for attributes like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.09,
          "end": 74.76,
          "en": "You typically only use it between tags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.76,
          "end": 76.41,
          "en": "as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.41,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "Instead, in cases like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 82.32,
          "en": "if you want to configure an element through its attributes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.32,
          "end": 86.07,
          "en": "you would typically use another core Angular feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.07,
          "end": 90.48,
          "en": "called property binding, which looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.48,
          "end": 92.7,
          "en": "You don't have curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.7,
          "end": 96.84,
          "en": "instead you wrap the name of the property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.84,
          "end": 100.97999999999999,
          "en": "of the DOM element you want to configure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.97999999999999,
          "end": 103.62,
          "en": "so of this image element, in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.62,
          "end": 106.41,
          "en": "You wrap the name of the property that should be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.41,
          "end": 108.69,
          "en": "with square brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.69,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "so opening and closing square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 113.163,
          "en": "around the property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.27000000000001,
          "end": 116.88,
          "en": "And then inside of those quotes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 121.5,
          "en": "you set the value that should be assigned to this property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.5,
          "end": 123.513,
          "en": "without curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 128.97,
          "en": "Now, selectedUser.avatar is actually not entirely correct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.97,
          "end": 132.3,
          "en": "because those images are stored in the assets folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.3,
          "end": 134.73,
          "en": "and they are in the users folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.73,
          "end": 137.76,
          "en": "so the image name alone is not enough,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.76,
          "end": 141.27,
          "en": "and that's why we here actually want to construct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.27,
          "end": 142.65,
          "en": "a dynamic path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.65,
          "end": 146.91,
          "en": "and concatenate that with selectedUser.avatar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.91,
          "end": 150.87,
          "en": "And then in that string created with single quotes here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.87,
          "end": 154.56,
          "en": "since I'm using double quotes to wrap the overall value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.56,
          "end": 159.56,
          "en": "we set up the rest of the path which is assets/users/",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 164.013,
          "en": "and then the name of the user image file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.09,
          "end": 168.87,
          "en": "And that is something you can do in Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.87,
          "end": 172.32,
          "en": "You cannot just reference properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.32,
          "end": 175.77,
          "en": "in places where you reference dynamic data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.77,
          "end": 179.4,
          "en": "but you can also create dynamic values just in time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.4,
          "end": 181.98,
          "en": "so to say, as I'm doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.98,
          "end": 185.22,
          "en": "by constructing a string from a fixed string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.22,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "that's then combined with that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 191.527,
          "en": "that's stored in the avatar property of the selectedUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.57,
          "end": 194.67,
          "en": "And we could have done something similar down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.67,
          "end": 197.55,
          "en": "with string interpolation as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.55,
          "end": 199.98,
          "en": "You can also have other JavaScript expressions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 203.16,
          "en": "like 1 + 1 in there if you needed it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 203.16,
          "end": 206.49,
          "en": "But in most cases, you will indeed refer to properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.49,
          "end": 209.13,
          "en": "and any values stored inside of them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 209.13,
          "end": 211.47,
          "en": "just as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.47,
          "end": 214.23,
          "en": "Well, and with that, to finish this image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 214.23,
          "end": 219.23,
          "en": "I also wanna bind the alt property on the image tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 219.84,
          "end": 221.94,
          "en": "on the image element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.94,
          "end": 226.763,
          "en": "and I'll bind this to selectedUser.name again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 227.67000000000002,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "And then I'll press the code formatting shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 232.44,
          "en": "that's built into Visual Studio Code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.44,
          "end": 234.87,
          "en": "so that the code gets formatted like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.87,
          "end": 236.703,
          "en": "and is a bit easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.35,
          "end": 241.02,
          "en": "And with all that done, if you now save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.02,
          "end": 243.33,
          "en": "you should see that if you now reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 243.33,
          "end": 246.18,
          "en": "you also got a image here next to that name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.18,
          "end": 249.3,
          "en": "that changes with every reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.3,
          "end": 252.42,
          "en": "And that is how you can output dynamic data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.42,
          "end": 254.58,
          "en": "in your Angular apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 254.58,
          "end": 257.94,
          "en": "and string interpolation and property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 257.94,
          "end": 261.06,
          "en": "are two of the most important features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.06,
          "end": 263.85,
          "en": "you have to know when working with Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 263.85,
          "end": 268.41,
          "en": "because in the end, Angular is all about building dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.41,
          "end": 270.51,
          "en": "interactive web applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.51,
          "end": 273.27,
          "en": "and that of course implies that you must be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.27,
          "end": 275.253,
          "en": "to output dynamic data.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
